we need to allow custom serializers to create an object.

example set of classes:

```
TBaseItemClass = class
  // some shared fields and virtual-abstract methods
end;

TSomeBaseItemClass = class(TBaseItemClass)
  // additional fields, virtual methods implementation, etc;
end;

TSomeAnotherBaseItemClass = class(TSomeBaseItemClass)
  // additional fields, virtual methods implementation, etc;
end;


THost = class
  FArrayField: TArray<TBaseItemClass>
end;

```

so, for example, i have THost instance with bunch of elements in FArrayField. (TSomeBaseItemClass, TSomeAnotherBaseItemClass instances)

i can seiralize THost w/o any problems.
but. during deserialization we will figure out that ReadArray/ReadDynArray using ElementType to create class instances.  so, array will be filled with TBaseItemClass intances.

its much better to use custom deserializer instead of TRttiUtils.CreateNewValue. 
at least custom deserializer will able to construct needed class by presence of fields. or we can add metadata to target json during serialization and use them during deserialization to construct needed class instance.

